SUBJECTIVE

Chief Complaint: My stomach is tearing apart, but I would rather die here than let those doctors touch me or force me into something I don't want.
History of Present Illness: The patient describes a chronic history of profound anticipatory autonomy loss anxiety regarding their reproductive health. Recently, due to legislative hypervigilance concerning changes restricting reproductive healthcare access, the patient has experienced escalating emotional exhaustion and a deep-seated obstetric mistrust. Over the past 12 hours, this stress has culminated in severe somatic manifestations, specifically acute, severe dysmenorrhea/pelvic floor tension and intractable nausea. The patient expresses anger and helplessness stemming from systemic attempts to control reproductive choices, financial dread related to out-of-pocket costs, and feelings of dehumanization during previous clinical encounters. They also report a chronic, paralyzing fear of forced birth or criminalization of pregnancy outcomes, which directly caused today's extreme care avoidance.
Functional Status: Acutely functionally impaired; writhing in bed, unable to stand upright due to pelvic pain and panic.
Social/Safety Concerns: High risk of preventable severe morbidity or mortality (e.g., undiagnosed ectopic rupture) due to profound, trauma-driven avoidance of emergency obstetric care.

