ASSESSMENT

Primary Diagnosis: Acute Severe Dysmenorrhea / Pelvic Floor Spasm complicated by Reproductive Justice / Autonomy Distress - Adjustment Disorder - V65.49 - Status: Exacerbated
Differentials:

Ruptured Ectopic Pregnancy - Ruled out/unlikely as the primary immediate threat given the absence of profound hypotension/shock, no shoulder tip pain, and the pain being bilateral and cramping rather than unilateral and sudden tearing, though an urgent ultrasound is still mandated.

